      "commit": {
        "parents": [
          {
            "commit": "89787fa29b1febed5ccf2380ad5519f0bd04d36d",
            "subject": "LU-21103 lov: move EC raid set code out of lov_io.c"
          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Keguang Xu",
          "email": "kxu@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-11-05 11:38:02.000000000",
          "tz": 480
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Keguang Xu",
          "email": "kxu@ddn.com",
          "date": "2026-11-05 11:45:53.000000000",
          "tz": 480
        },
        "subject": "LU-21103 lov: decide a raid set's unavailable stripes once",
        "message": "LU-21103 lov: decide a raid set's unavailable stripes once\n\nlov_ec_io_route() and lov_ecio_add_data_sub() each count a raid set's\ndead and slow-marked stripes, take its parity budget and compare the\ntwo, so a change to which stripes a reconstruction skips has to be\nmade twice and kept in step.\n\nAdd lov_ec_raid_set_decide(), which counts the stripes, takes the\nbudget only when a stripe is unavailable, and says whether the set's\ndead and its slow stripes are skipped.  Both callers use it.\nlov_ec_io_route() folds the raid sets with an ordered enum\nlov_ec_set_fit instead of four flags.  The load check stays in\nlov_ec_io_route() alone; a comment in lov_ecio_add_data_sub() says\nwhy: a reconstruction reads every stripe of the raid set anyway, so\nthe set's load does not change which of its stripes to skip.\nlov_ec_set_parity_budget() and lov_ec_raid_set_count() become static.\n\nAlso give the soft deadline of a read extent one implementation,\nosc_extent_soft_tmo(), for osc_queue_dio_pages() and\nosc_queue_sync_pages(), keeping the rules of each.\n\nNo functional change.\n\nTest-Parameters: ignore\nSigned-off-by: Keguang Xu <kxu@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: Augment Agent:Claude Opus 5.5\nChange-Id: I526fe4bfadc26b740eece2782cf6c39420c42962\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
